Count BLAKE2s compressions behind a `count-ops` feature.

Part of the verifier-only build of SASH eb95bfa that the SP1 segment guest runs
(verifiable-inference-ethereum SPEC.md §1.1). Upstream source is Apache-2.0;
this patch modifies it (Apache-2.0 §4(b)).

SP1 has no BLAKE2s precompile, so no syscall count gives the verifier's BLAKE2s
share. All of SASH's BLAKE2s goes through `hash_node` (blake2_merkle.rs) and
`Blake2sHasherGeneric` (blake2_hash.rs, which the channel and `mix_root` use).
A native host measurement build turns the feature on to count them; the guest
never does, and with the feature off the build is unchanged.

- nitroo/crates/stwo/Cargo.toml: a `count-ops` feature, off by default.
- nitroo/crates/stwo/src/core/vcs/count_ops.rs (new): a counting wrapper around
  `blake2::Blake2s256` that adds `max(1, ceil(n / 64))` compressions per hash
  at finalize, `n` the bytes absorbed, to one counter per site (`hash_node`,
  channel). Never per `update` call: `hash_node` calls it once per 4-byte M31.
- nitroo/crates/stwo/src/core/vcs/blake2_merkle.rs, blake2_hash.rs: the
  `use blake2::{Blake2s256, Digest};` line becomes, on the same line, a
  `#[cfg(not(feature = "count-ops"))]` / `#[cfg(feature = "count-ops")]` pair
  importing `Blake2s256` from blake2 or from count_ops. No other line moves:
  the panic sites of blake2_hash.rs embed their line in the guest ELF.
- nitroo/crates/stwo/src/core/vcs/mod.rs: one line appended, declaring
  count_ops under the feature.

